# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# WHITELIST MODE — ignore everything, then allow specific paths
# This prevents accidentally pushing local-only files to GitHub.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Step 1: Ignore everything
/*

# Step 2: Allow tracked directories (un-ignore with !)
!Templates/

# Step 3: Allow repo config files
!.gitignore
!.claude/
!README.md
!CONTRIBUTING.md
!CLAUDE.md

# Step 4: Within allowed directories, still exclude build artifacts
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/

# Step 5: Exclude personal/local files even in allowed dirs
.claude/settings.local.json

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SAFE TO RUN: git add .
# Only Templates/ and repo config files will be staged.
# Everything else (Analysis_Report, PaperWork_Design_Src, Work_Reports,
# Backups, Src, etc.) is automatically ignored.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
